                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "47adf658-8502-3b22-b03a-2237b23510b5",
                        "entry_id": "d1c01f5a-33f3-3335-b464-05f34957ceb0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To emit smoke."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "efd12f4f-e701-4c52-9b35-f1917ff8f418",
                                "sense_id": "47adf658-8502-3b22-b03a-2237b23510b5",
                                "text": "18th c, Robert Burns, The Twa Dogs, 1822, The Poetical Works of Robert Burns, page 28,\nThe lunting pipe, and sneeshing mill, / Are handed round wi' right gude-will;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d203e1ef-6017-4b71-ba01-0a125be08976",
                                "sense_id": "47adf658-8502-3b22-b03a-2237b23510b5",
                                "text": "My conscience! ye lent a ready hand in the brulzie; but what can ha'e set the Magazines a-lunting? it's a mystery o' mysteries.[…]Especially as it's their game to set everybody a-lunting, and keep out of the conflagration themselves."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "913b89e2-c11b-3521-b256-e60248ee931a",
                        "entry_id": "d1c01f5a-33f3-3335-b464-05f34957ceb0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To walk while smoking a pipe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb6d4d7c-e355-4357-b8e4-6f3eb162b01e",
                                "sense_id": "913b89e2-c11b-3521-b256-e60248ee931a",
                                "text": "2014, Robert P. Wills, Tales From A Second Hand Wand Shoppe, Book 1: They Were the Best of Gnomes, They Were the Worst of Gnomes, page 278,\n“Lunting?” interrupted Julie, eyebrow raised.\nGrimbledung shrugged, “It's a good and proper word”, he raised an eyebrow back, \"it just doesn't get used that much.\"\nJulie smirked, “Go on then, with your lunting.”\nHe let out a sigh. \"As I was saying, I was sitting there when a Minotaur came lunting up.\" He paused for a moment, \"Pipe in mouth, walking along\", he winked at Julie, […] ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
